comments.body:
I think the direct handler calls here (the `CallOneOf` over `protocolinfo_cb` … `add_onion_cb`) hide the paths that need the wire. As far as I tested, no input got past PROTOCOLINFO over the wire.

Suggestion from my clanker:

`FakeTor` records the verb of each command it sees in `ProcessCommands()`. A new operation answers the oldest unanswered command with a reply of the matching shape (code usually 250, sometimes one of `CODES`). It reuses the existing line generators, which are split out of `ConsumeReplyLine()`. All existing operations stay. The direct-call operation is also gated behind one extra `ConsumeBool()`.

